'''Tal Merrik''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] [[prince]] who [[Senator|represented]] his [[homeworld]] of [[Kalevala]] in the [[Galactic Senate]] during the [[Clone Wars]], and served as a member of the Galactic Senate's [[Council of Neutral Systems]]. Merrik secretly worked alongside [[Death Watch]], a group of [[Mandalorian]]s who disagreed with the pacifist ways of the [[New Mandalorians]], and sought to usurp [[Duchess]] [[Satine Kryze]]. Merrik's [[Skirmish aboard the Coronet|attempt]] on Kryze's life brought him into contact with [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]], the latter of whom [[Death|killed]] Merrik aboard the ''[[Coronet]]''.

==Biography==
===Alongside Satine===
{{Quote|I know we sound defensive, but&mdash;|Merrik, before being cut off by Satine|<ref name="TMP" />}}
A [[Gender|male]] [[human]],<ref name="TMP" /> Tal Merrik served his [[homeworld]] of [[Kalevala]],<ref name="SWE" /> a [[planet]] in the [[Mandalore system]],<ref name="KalevalaDB">{{Databank|kalevala|Kalevala}}</ref> in the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Galactic Senate|Senate]].<ref name="TMP" /> However, in secret, Merrik was working with the [[Mandalorian]] [[terrorist]] organization known as [[Death Watch]], and due to this, also the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="VoT" /> Operating beneath the leadership of [[Pre Vizsla]], who led a double life as governor of [[Concordia]], the Death Watch sought to overthrow the New Mandalorians and re-establish the warlike culture of their past. Already sympathetic to these ambitions, despite his long friendship with Duchess Satine Kryze, Tal Merrik also had shady political goals that made the business of becoming a turncoat a simple matter.<ref name="TalMerrikDB">{{Databank|tal-merrik|Tal Merrik}}</ref>

[[File:New_Mandalorians.png|thumb|left|250px|Merrik stands beside Kryze]]
Merrik was seen walking alongside [[Satine Kryze]] on [[Mandalore]] in the [[Sundari Royal Palace]], during the [[time]] she greeted [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], an [[emissary]] from the [[Jedi High Council]] who was investigating rumors of Mandalorian involvement with the Separatists. He was also noticeably surprised when Kryze retorted against Kenobi, whose government accused her of [[treason]] against the Republic. Merrik attempted to speak to Kenobi and [[Prime Minister]] [[Almec]] before Kryze interrupted him and engaged in a battle of words with Kenobi. Kenobi revealed his mission was assigned by the [[Jedi]] Council, silencing Kryze, who had believed him to be on assignment from the Republic. Kryze and Kenobi then departed on a walk through the [[Domed city|domed]] [[capital]] [[city]] of Mandalore, [[Sundari]].<ref name="TMP" />

===The ''Coronet''===
====Interrupting debates====
[[File:ObiWanAndSatineDebate.png|thumb|right|250px|Kenobi and Kryze's debate is interrupted by Taa]]
{{Quote|Duchess, Master Jedi. It's been a long trip. I think we could all use a little rest and refreshment.|Tal Merrik|<ref name="VoT" />}}
Merrik later was present on the ''[[Coronet]]'', a luxury [[starship]] used to take members of the [[Council of Neutral Systems]] to the [[The galaxy|galactic]] capital world [[Coruscant]]. Kenobi, [[Jedi Knight]] [[Anakin Skywalker]] and several [[clone trooper]]s were also aboard as protection against a Death Watch threat. Merrik questioned the [[Duchess]] on how the Council would oppose the [[Clone Wars]]. Kenobi entered the room and entered a follow-up debate with Kryze on the merits of Jedi involvement in the war, before being interrupted by [[Orn Free Taa]]. Merrik and Taa agreed that both Kryze and Kenobi proved there were two sides to every dilemma.<ref name="VoT" />

Later, Kenobi and Kryze continued their debate, which Merrik interrupted once more, stating that they could all use rest and refreshments. Kryze then promptly left the room, as the others, including [[Kin Robb]] and [[Onaconda Farr]], observed in silence.<ref name="VoT" />

====An interruption at dinner====
{{Quote|Obi-Wan, there's assassin probes down here. One made it up the lift, I'll try to hold the others down here.''"<br />"''Quickly! Secure the lifts!|Skywalker and Kenobi, shortly before the assassin probe arrived at dinner service|<ref name="VoT" />}}
[[File:Epguide213.jpg|thumb|left|260px|Kenobi defends the senators]]
Farr, Kryze, Robb, Merrik and Taa shared dinner, which included deep-fried [[nuna]] leg, aboard the ''Coronet''. Kenobi entered the room and announced to the [[senator]]s that the [[Cloning|clones]] were investigating a disturbance below decks. Merrik observed as Kenobi received a call on his [[comlink]] that revealed a container had been opened and emptied. Inside the container were [[SD-K4 assassin droid|assassin probes]], one of which was dispatched in the lower levels while a second had escaped up the [[Turbolift|elevator]]. The second [[assassin]] probe arrived at the dinner service quickly and prepared to attack the senators before Kenobi dispatched it.<ref name="VoT" />

However, the assassin probes spouted smaller [[SD-K4a mini-assassin droid]]s that swarmed the room. Kenobi used his [[lightsaber]] to destroy many, whilst Kryze utilized her [[blaster pistol]] to deactivate them. After somewhat returning to dinner service, Kenobi arrived with one of the probe killers in a container. Kenobi used the probe to see which senator it would not attack, revealing the traitor. When Kenobi realized that Merrik was the [[treason]]ous one, Merrik quickly retaliated and took Kryze hostage.<ref name="VoT" />

====Taking the Duchess hostage====
{{Quote|Tal Merrik, you are under arrest. Release the Duchess.''"<br />"''Hmm. I took the precaution of wiring this ship's engines to explode. I press this remote, and we ''all'' die.|Kenobi and Merrik|<ref name="VoT" />}}
[[File:TalMerrickTraitor.png|thumb|right|250px|Merrik takes Kryze hostage]]
Merrik held a [[Weequay blaster pistol|blaster]] to Kryze's head and took the Duchess from the dinner room, arriving at the helm of the ship, where he quickly dispatched all the [[pilot]]s and contacted [[Pre Vizsla]]. Death Watch informed him that reinforcements were on the way, just as three [[Droch-class boarding ship|''Droch''-class boarding ships]] carrying [[B2-series super battle droid]]s arrived on the ''Coronet''. Merrik, who had secretly wired the starship's [[engine]]s to explode at the press of a button, threatened Kenobi as a fight ensued across the ship as the droids attacked the clone troopers and [[Journeyman Protector|Mandalorian Protectors]].<ref name="VoT" />

===Death===
{{Quote|Come on, then! Who will strike first and brand themselves a cold-blooded killer?|Merrik, just prior to his death|audio=MerrikLastWords.flac|<ref name="VoT" />}}
[[File:TalMerrickFate.png|thumb|left|200px|Merrik is killed by Anakin Skywalker]]
As Merrik made his way to escape, Kryze expressed her love for Kenobi, who did the same, much to Merrik's chagrin, before she insulted Merrik, calling him a [[Slug (creature)|slug]] for his betrayal, stepping on his [[Limb|foot]] and taking his blaster. As they both pointed their weapons at him, Merrik expressed amusement that neither of them would [[Death|kill]] him, as Kryze would be branded a hypocrite to all of her pacifist ideals and Kenobi would be seen as a hero to everyone but the Duchess, who would be disgusted. Merrik then tauntingly asked who would brand themselves a killer in striking him first. Neither of them killed him; instead, Anakin Skywalker snuck up behind the unsuspecting senator and killed him with a lightsaber through the chest.<ref name="VoT" />

===Legacy===
Merrik's dreams of Mandalore switching sides would eventually be fulfilled when Death Watch [[Takeover of Mandalore|conquered]] Mandalore two [[Standard year|years]] later.<ref name="Shades of Reason">{{TCW|Shades of Reason}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
Tal Merrik first appeared in "[[The Mandalore Plot]]," the twelfth episode of ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''' [[The Clone Wars: Season Two|second season]]. His identity was confirmed in the credits. He was voiced by [[Greg Proops]], who voiced [[Fodesinbeed Annodue|Fode]] in [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="TMP" />

Concept art of the character was done by [[Bosco Ng]].<ref name="Tumblr">{{Tumblr|subdomain=starwars|name=''Star Wars''|url=post/107552682613/artist-of-the-week-bosco-ng|text=Artist of the Week - Bosco Ng|archivedate=20210126205156}}</ref> An early model of Merrik seems to depict the character as female; using an existing generic female Mandalorian citizen asset as a basis.<ref name="CCA EG3">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/corruption-concept-art-gallery|text="Corruption" Concept Art Gallery}} {{C|Slide 3}}</ref>

